</div> </div> </div>In the comics it makes more sense","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T18:50:25-07:00","id":1215308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1215294-avengers-infinity-war-spoiler-talk?p=1215297#post1215297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the comics it makes more sense</div> </div> </div> </div>For a certain value of &quot;sense&quot; I guess. I think it is <i>at least</i> as insane as in the movie. I mean, it makes some twisted sort of sense to gift your the one you love with the deaths of half the universe when you are trying to win the love of literally death incarnate. &quot;I am in love with the cosmic incarnation of death&quot;, however, is very insane.<br /> <br /> That said, at least then you couldn't plausibly tell him &quot;well, if you are so worried about resource shortages, surely you can use that Infinite power of yours to turn every society in the universe into a post-scarcity one by supplying impossible, infinite resources, right?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T19:06:01-07:00","id":1215312,"title":"","content":"Killing off enough people to impress the hot goddess of death across the room makes way more sense than killing half the universe's population due to a problem that isn't actually quite the problem people think it is when you have the god-like-power to <i>create infinite resources</i>.<br /> <br /> Movie Thanos is stupid, and I haven't even seen the movie yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T19:17:47-07:00","id":1215319,"title":"","content":"...I'm kind of hoping one of the writers realizes this, and makes specific mention of it in Avengers 4, using it to highlight just how messed up Thanos is. The power of infinity at his literal fingertips, and his first and only thought is to destroy.<br /> <br /> Might make that work, I don't know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T20:04:22-07:00","id":1215327,"title":"","content":"Yeah, his plan is dumb as hell, but the movie was cool otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T20:09:16-07:00","id":1215328,"title":"","content":"I think you're all forgetting that Thanos' official title is &quot;The <b>Mad</b> Titan&quot; so of course he's not going to be acting in the right state of mind.<br /> <br /> <br /> I mean, you guys remember what he was like <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pTKYmGV5pB4\" target=\"_blank\">back in the cartoons</a>, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 05-04-2018, 11:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T20:19:55-07:00","id":1215329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1215294-avengers-infinity-war-spoiler-talk?p=1215328#post1215328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you're all forgetting that Thanos' official title is &quot;The <b>Mad</b> Titan&quot; so of course he's not going to be acting in the right state of mind.<br /> <br /> <br /> I mean, you guys remember what he was like <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pTKYmGV5pB4\" target=\"_blank\">back in the cartoons</a>, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a terrible excuse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T21:31:11-07:00","id":1215343,"title":"","content":"Just finished. I think my entire body is shaking. <br /> <br /> I almost gave the screen the finger at the &quot;Thanos will return&quot; after the stinger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T21:50:10-07:00","id":1215351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1215294-avengers-infinity-war-spoiler-talk?p=1215329#post1215329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is a terrible excuse.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But an accurate one....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T22:00:32-07:00","id":1215357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1215294-avengers-infinity-war-spoiler-talk?p=1215351#post1215351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> But an accurate one....</div> </div> </div> </div>No. No it's not.<br /> <br /> Disregarding all the ways that mad is a loaded term, mad narratively does not mean internally incoherent and unsatisfying. The comic book Thanos is, at least, satisfying with his &quot;insane&quot; desire and plan, and it has a consistency. Nolan/BTAS Joker is &quot;mad&quot;, but his actions actually do parse out to his desires that is satisfying for the audience to follow on.<br /> <br /> It takes less than a second of looking at Thanos's plan and goal before you realize that even an &quot;insane&quot; person would realize that that's a waste of a god's powers.<br /> <br /> We do not have to look far to see how weak &quot;madness&quot; is as an excuse, and, honestly, it's a poor one. He's <i>too</i> coherent and together to really sell &quot;madness&quot;. This is not a madman. This is a cheap attempt to make a simple but effective character more morally complex and dropping the ball because no one thought about what infinite cosmic power actually means.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T22:04:37-07:00","id":1215358,"title":"","content":"Cheesy anime OVA's with more focus on how to squeeze in panty shots than actual narrative coherence have plots less stupid attributed to the villains goals. I am just saying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T22:08:14-07:00","id":1215361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1215294-avengers-infinity-war-spoiler-talk?p=1215357#post1215357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. No it's not.<br /> <br /> Disregarding all the ways that mad is a loaded term, mad narratively does not mean internally incoherent and unsatisfying. The comic book Thanos is, at least, satisfying with his &quot;insane&quot; desire and plan, and it has a consistency. Nolan/BTAS Joker is &quot;mad&quot;, but his actions actually do parse out to his desires that is satisfying for the audience to follow on.<br /> <br /> It takes less than a second of looking at Thanos's plan and goal before you realize that even an &quot;insane&quot; person would realize that that's a waste of a god's powers.<br /> <br /> We do not have to look far to see how weak &quot;madness&quot; is as an excuse, and, honestly, it's a poor one. He's <i>too</i> coherent and together to really sell &quot;madness&quot;. This is not a madman. This is a cheap attempt to make a simple but effective character more morally complex and dropping the ball because no one thought about what infinite cosmic power actually means.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> So wait, people are upset that Thanos only wiped out half the universe instead of all of it? Because if I'm not mistaken, that's exactly what he did in the comics, too.<br /> <br /> And the reason Thanos failed in those is because he subconsciously believed that he wasn't actually worthy of succeeding. This allowed his enemies to steal the gauntlet from him and then Adam Warlock used its power to fix everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 05-05-2018, 01:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T22:11:27-07:00","id":1215362,"title":"","content":"My partner says that Thanos <i>killed</i> after movie scenes. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T22:28:01-07:00","id":1215368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1215294-avengers-infinity-war-spoiler-talk?p=1215361#post1215361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> So wait, people are upset that Thanos only wiped out half the universe instead of all of it? Because if I'm not mistaken, that's exactly what he did in the comics, too.<br /> <br /> <br /> And look on the bright side, this might give Marvel the opportunity to bring new characters into the movies, such as Captain Marvel, or Adam Warlock. Maybe we'll get to see the Kree Empire, or the Skrulls?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Wiping out half the universe is not the problem. From what I hear, the finger snapping thing is actually pretty cool.<br /> <br /> The problem is that his plan(wipe out half the universe's population) to solve the problem(resource depletion leading to overpopulation leading to war and strife leading to suffering, ANAKIN) when the resources he is collecting (the Infinity Stones) allow for an easier, more heroic alternative(infinite cosmic power used to create infinite resources therefore eliminating any conflict due to overpopulation) makes him look like a <i>fucking idiot</i>. It doesn't even look <i>insane</i>, just <i>incredibly stupid</i>.<br /> <br /> They wanted to make Thanos the hero of his own story, with a goal and ambition worthy of someone worth all god damn 19+3 movies. Cool, storytelling 101, solid villain base to work from, modern edgy audiences really love that shit. But by doing so <i>poorly</i>, they have neither delivered that, thereby disappointing the movie goers, nor did they deliver the admittedly goofy but still elementally brutal and powerful comic book version of the character, which pisses off the comic book fans. And that latter one, while simple, probably would have been a thrill for movie audiences as well, just simply because he is so elementally overpowering as a presence and an effect.<br /> <br /> They promised a villain worthy of a franchise and gave us a narratively bankrupt caricature. While I understand the presentation is fucking stellar, the simple fact of the matter is that everything about him falls apart in seconds with an iota of thought, and that sours the experience for people looking back and hardens the hearts of people going in, making future investment into the movie that much harder.<br /> <br /> \u200bI'm sure it'll be fun. But I don't plan on taking Thanos remotely seriously.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Like, by contrast, comic book Thanos:<br /> <br /> Plan: Wipe out half the Universe Population<br /> Goal: Get with that sweet, sweet Death.<br /> Resources: Infinity Stones, aka Infinite Cosmic Power<br /> <br /> At that point, the only question left is &quot;Why only half&quot;, and when you are cosmic genocidal asshole with infinite cosmic power killing people to impress that sweet, sweet Death, you pretty much have every right to answer &quot;eh, who gives a shit&quot; and their only recourse is to just go with it because what are they going to do on that point with you.<br /> <br /> \u200bThere's a contrast here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 05-05-2018, 01:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T22:32:06-07:00","id":1215370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1215294-avengers-infinity-war-spoiler-talk?p=1215361#post1215361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So wait, people are upset that Thanos only wiped out half the universe instead of all of it? Because if I'm not mistaken, that's exactly what he did in the comics, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, people are upset because Marvel decided that since Thanos wiped out half the universe in the comics, they were going to have him do that in the movies, but rather than sticking with his motivation for doing so in the comics, they changed it to \u201che believes it will save the universe from overpopulation,\u201d disregarding the fact that he could have just as easily used the power of the infinity gauntlet to fix that problem by just magically making enough resources for everyone. By changing his motive, they made his methods stupid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 05-05-2018, 01:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T22:55:28-07:00","id":1215378,"title":"","content":"So, Thanos\u2019 nonsense motive aside, I\u2019d like to bring up another point I took issue with.<br /> <br /> Maybe it\u2019s because I haven\u2019t read the comics and am therefore unfamiliar with the infinity stones and the limits of their powers, but... They seemed incredibly inconsistent to me. If Thanos could use the time stone to rewind time <i>just for Vision</i> to repair the Mind Stone, why couldn\u2019t Doctor Strange rewind time just for Thanos on Titan so he would have still been under the antenna lady\u2019s mind power and wouldn\u2019t have escaped? Like, I get that I\u2019m supposed to accept that the future where Thanos gets all of the stones is the only one Doctor Strange saw where they (eventually) win, but that\u2019s a hard pill to swallow when they were seconds from separating Thanos\u2019 glove from him and didn\u2019t just use their time travel device to go back a sec and like... punch Starlord, or hell, just cut Thanos\u2019 arm off instead of trying to pull off his glove or something. And if Thanos can use the reality Stone to turn what ever he wants into bubbles, what the hell is he blasting everyone with purple energy for, instead of, you know, turning them into bubbles? Maybe him using the gauntlet to kill half the universe instead of doubling its resources isn\u2019t so inconsistent after all - he seems to make really stupid use of his phenomenal cosmic powers pretty regularly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T22:59:24-07:00","id":1215380,"title":"","content":"Admittedly, if there is one thing we should have all learned way back with Avengers 1, it's that these movies prize spectacle over...well, pretty much everything else.<br /> <br /> But, uh, yeah. Infinite Cosmic Power is not exactly something people play with well when rubber meets the road.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T23:04:42-07:00","id":1215381,"title":"","content":"Oh, real quick, can anyone with more Marvel knowledge than me fill me in on why Red Skull was guarding the soul stone? I felt like I was missing something, but I\u2019m a very fair weather MCU watcher, so I assume I actually was just missing something that was set up in another film I didn\u2019t see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T01:07:59-07:00","id":1215397,"title":"","content":"At the end of the first Captain America movie Red Skull sort of got sucked into the Tesseract/Space Stone. Apparently it spat him out to be a guardian.<br /> <br /> That's not an aspect that's from the comics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T05:08:23-07:00","id":1215448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1215294-avengers-infinity-war-spoiler-talk?p=1215378#post1215378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, Thanos\u2019 nonsense motive aside, I\u2019d like to bring up another point I took issue with.<br /> <br /> Maybe it\u2019s because I haven\u2019t read the comics and am therefore unfamiliar with the infinity stones and the limits of their powers, but... They seemed incredibly inconsistent to me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Infinity Stones are like control panels for reality itself. True to their name, they possess <b>infinite</b> <b>power</b> over their designated purview, that being Time, Mind, Space, Reality, Power or Soul. They only have two known weaknesses.<br /> <br /> The first being that each set of Infinity Stones only functions within the universe that they originate from. You can't steal one universe's set and wield them in a different one.<br /> <br /> Their second weakness is they can't be used to destroy themselves. This is because the Infinity Stones are connected to what they manipulate. Destroying the Time stone, for example, would destroy time itself.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>The Living Tribunal </b>is one such being, since he's a multiversal entity and the herald for the <b>One Above All</b>, who is basically an in universe personification for the writers of Marvel.<br /> <br /> <br /> If you want a more thorough explanation of their abilities, <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1Z9fReGWArU\" target=\"_blank\">this video might help</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 05-05-2018, 08:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T06:23:32-07:00","id":1215461,"title":"","content":"Enjoyed the film, immensely! And Thanos was a great <u><b>villain</b></u>(which the MCU needed).<br /> <br /> Maybe people can write their own fanfics of Thanos being a hero by using the gauntlet for good, rather than evil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":95,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","user":"Fat Larry","date":". 05-05-2018, 09:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T06:31:26-07:00","id":1215465,"title":"","content":"Because of course people never get their thoughts locked into patterns, effectively indoctrinating themselves. Surely it is simply impossible for a person to have irrational motives strengthened by fanatic beliefs that blind them to what they can, cannot, should, and should not do. I mean, it never happens in real life, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T07:01:37-07:00","id":1215471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1215294-avengers-infinity-war-spoiler-talk?p=1215461#post1215461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Enjoyed the film, immensely! And Thanos was a great <u><b>villain</b></u>(which the MCU needed).<br /> <br /> Maybe people can write their own fanfics of Thanos being a hero by using the gauntlet for good, rather than evil.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, the motive they chose for him <i>was</i> good. He wanted to save the universe from overpopulation, and killing have the people in it is just a nonsense way to go about doing that when you have infinite power.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s not his methods themes I object to. It\u2019s the fact that his methods don\u2019t make sense for his motive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T07:02:11-07:00","id":1215472,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=21C Hermit;n1215465]Because of course people never get their thoughts locked into patterns, effectively indoctrinating themselves. Surely it is simply impossible for a person to have irrational motives strengthened by fanatic beliefs that blind them to what they can, cannot, should, and should not do. I mean, it never happens in real life, right?[/QUOTE<br /> <br /> NO! We MUST pick apart movies at every step!!! ARGHHHHHHHHH! I hate Ant-Man because what he does is impossible! ARGHHHHH!<br /> <br /> *runs and bus tickets to see Jurassic World. <br /> <br /> My favorite &quot;superhero movie guy,&quot; is the one who tells you step-by-step, what they would've done in a fight. Like, how &quot;A superhero, should've done this when fighting B superhero.&quot;<br /> <br /> Like, dude, have you ever been in a fight? That's not how things work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T07:05:54-07:00","id":1215473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1215294-avengers-infinity-war-spoiler-talk?p=1215471#post1215471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The thing is, the motive they chose for him <i>was</i> good. He wanted to save the universe from overpopulation, and killing have the people in it is just a nonsense way to go about doing that when you have infinite power.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s not his methods themes I object to. It\u2019s the fact that his methods don\u2019t make sense for his motive.</div> </div> </div> </div>His methods involve torture and execution. Gamora stated such, numerous times(in Avengers and GotG). <br /> <br /> Thanos is NOT a good guy. He's not a hero. Never has been. Not in the comics, not in the films. Starlin wanted him to be an insane monster--worse than Darkseid(who he was modeled after). <br /> <br /> I'd say Infinity War and Josh Brolin captured that well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T07:12:32-07:00","id":1215474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1215294-avengers-infinity-war-spoiler-talk?p=1215378#post1215378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe him using the gauntlet to kill half the universe instead of doubling its resources isn\u2019t so inconsistent after all - he seems to make really stupid use of his phenomenal cosmic powers pretty regularly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe that'll happen in the next movie. Deadpool will show up and ask, &quot;So Thanos. How come you decided to wipe out half of all life in the universe instead of doing X?&quot;<br /> <br /> And Thanos will put his hand on his chin and get really introspective for a few moments, maybe pace and forth and then say, &quot;Oh jeeze, uhhh... that <i>was</i> an option, wasn't it? I am so sorry everyone. Really. Ya know, it just never even occured to me to do that. Wow. This is just... whew. Really wish I'd considered that sooner because suddenly I feel like a real asshole. Man, talk about awkward.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T07:16:36-07:00","id":1215478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1215294-avengers-infinity-war-spoiler-talk?p=1215448#post1215448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The Infinity Stones are like control panels for reality itself. True to their name, they possess <b>infinite</b> <b>power</b> over their designated purview, that being Time, Mind, Space, Reality, Power or Soul. They only have two known weaknesses.<br /> <br /> The first being that each set of Infinity Stones only functions within the universe that they originate from. You can't steal one universe's set and wield them in a different one.<br /> <br /> Their second weakness is they can't be used to destroy themselves. This is because the Infinity Stones are connected to what they manipulate. Destroying the Time stone, for example, would destroy time itself.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>The Living Tribunal </b>is one such being, since he's a multiversal entity and the herald for the <b>One Above All</b>, who is basically an in universe personification for the writers of Marvel.<br /> <br /> <br /> If you want a more thorough explanation of their abilities, <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1Z9fReGWArU&amp;quot;]this</a> video might help[/URL].</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, so it\u2019s not just me. Doctor Strange has infinite power over time and instead of just using it to turn Thanos into a zygote or rewind the few extra seconds they needed to get the infinity gauntlet off of him, he... uhh... didn\u2019t do that thing. And Thanos, who had infinite power over space, power, and reality at that point decided to fight the folks on Titan with purple lasers instead of just turning them all into seven notes of music. And then after he did somehow get the time stone, he didn\u2019t just freeze time while he went to go get the mind stone. And when Thor attacked him he just let him embed his axe in his chest instead of making the axe disappear, or the distance to him too far for Thor\u2019s momentum to carry him. He had infinite power over mind and he never just made his enemies agree with him.<br /> <br /> See what I mean that they seem inconsistent? Like, I can\u2019t be too hard on the writers, infinite power over anything is very difficult to work with. But that makes the whole premise of the Infinity War kind of doomed to these issues of \u201chow does Thanos ever fail if he can control reality? How does he ever get to control reality if the good guys control time?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T07:17:11-07:00","id":1215479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1215294-avengers-infinity-war-spoiler-talk?p=1215471#post1215471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The thing is, the motive they chose for him <i>was</i> good. He wanted to save the universe from overpopulation, and killing have the people in it is just a nonsense way to go about doing that when you have infinite power.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s not his methods themes I object to. It\u2019s the fact that his methods don\u2019t make sense for his motive.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> People in real life did more nonsensical things for less noble motives. I see no reason for Thanos to meet higher standards than what we give to fanatics all across the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T07:21:01-07:00","id":1215480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1215294-avengers-infinity-war-spoiler-talk?p=1215478#post1215478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ok, so it\u2019s not just me. Doctor Strange has infinite power over time and instead of just using it to turn Thanos into a zygote or rewind the few extra seconds they needed to get the infinity gauntlet off of him, he... uhh... didn\u2019t do that thing. And Thanos, who had infinite power over space, power, and reality at that point decided to fight the folks on Titan with purple lasers instead of just turning them all into seven notes of music. And then after he did somehow get the time stone, he didn\u2019t just freeze time while he went to go get the mind stone. And when Thor attacked him he just let him embed his axe in his chest instead of making the axe disappear, or the distance to him too far for Thor\u2019s momentum to carry him. He had infinite power over mind and he never just made his enemies agree with him.<br /> <br /> See what I mean that they seem inconsistent? Like, I can\u2019t be too hard on the writers, infinite power over anything is very difficult to work with. But that makes the whole premise of the Infinity War kind of doomed to these issues of \u201chow does Thanos ever fail if he can control reality? How does he ever get to control reality if the good guys control time?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Nyrufa's clarification of the Stones having infinite power only works for the original comics. I see no reason why that needs to hold to the movies.<br /> <br /> And there's this old metaphor of an ocean and a bowl. Even if you have the ocean at your feet, you can only carry a bowl of water from it.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I think the words &quot;infinite&quot; and &quot;mad&quot; are inviting certain preconceptions here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T07:24:04-07:00","id":1215482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1215294-avengers-infinity-war-spoiler-talk?p=1215471#post1215471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is, the motive they chose for him <i>was</i> good. He wanted to save the universe from overpopulation, and killing have the people in it is just a nonsense way to go about doing that when you have infinite power.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's especially awkward when you look at population trends. Take the population growth rate of Earth. In 1970 we had a population of around 3.5 billion. It only took 50 years for the population of Earth to double. So even if he halved the population of Earth, and put us back to 1970's levels, it wouldn't take more than a century (and probably less than that) for the population to get back to where it was. And then it'll keep progressing rapidly just like it did before. Simply killing a bunch of people is not an effective long-term solution to overpopulation. <br /> <br /> It would have been more effective for him to use his infinite and unlimited power to lower the birth rate of living creatures - something like the Krogan Genophage from Mass Effect would have been a far, far more effective long term solution to overpopulation than just killing half of everybody. Sure you do that, but the population will recover and then exceed the original numbers in a couple of dozen decades. He basically bought the universe an extra 50 years when he could have bought the universe millennia. Great job you crazy old titan you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 05-05-2018, 10:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T07:25:54-07:00","id":1215483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1215294-avengers-infinity-war-spoiler-talk?p=1215473#post1215473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">His methods involve torture and execution. Gamora stated such, numerous times(in Avengers and GotG).</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, which is fine. I\u2019ve got no problem with villains using villainous methods.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1215294-avengers-infinity-war-spoiler-talk?p=1215473#post1215473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanos is NOT a good guy. He's not a hero. Never has been. Not in the comics, not in the films.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that, by his goals, he is in the film. He literally wants to save the universe. And I get the desire to give him a relatable goal and make his methods the thing that makes him evil. I bought it when he was trying to battle overpopulation by killing half of every planet\u2019s population by military conquest. The issue is, once he got a hold of unlimited power, he got a way to achieve his goal of stopping overpopulation without killing anyone.<br /> <br /> Now, you can say he\u2019s just evil and really wanted to kill half the universe and his overpopulation thing was just how he excused that to himself. But if that was the intent, it didn\u2019t come across. He just came across as an idiot who didn\u2019t realize infinite power could do more than shoot purple lazer beams and kill everyone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T07:33:38-07:00","id":1215486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1215294-avengers-infinity-war-spoiler-talk?p=1215479#post1215479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People in real life did more nonsensical things for less noble motives. I see no reason for Thanos to meet higher standards than what we give to fanatics all across the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, no, I buy the whole \u201ckill half of everyone to stop overpopulation\u201d thing when he had to do it by invading planets with his armies. That makes sense as being the most effective method to a warped mind. The problem is that once he has the infinity gauntlet and all six stones, he could just as easily snap his fingers and halve everyone\u2019s resource consumption rate, double the resources in the universe, double the size of every planet, whatever he wants. To someone who can literally do anything they want, killing half the universe only really makes sense if his goal is to kill half the universe. Which it was in the comics. They changed his motive without changing his methods, and in so doing made his methods no longer make sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T07:39:16-07:00","id":1215487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1215294-avengers-infinity-war-spoiler-talk?p=1215478#post1215478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ok, so it\u2019s not just me. Doctor Strange has infinite power over time and instead of just using it to turn Thanos into a zygote or rewind the few extra seconds they needed to get the infinity gauntlet off of him, he... uhh... didn\u2019t do that thing. And Thanos, who had infinite power over space, power, and reality at that point decided to fight the folks on Titan with purple lasers instead of just turning them all into seven notes of music. And then after he did somehow get the time stone, he didn\u2019t just freeze time while he went to go get the mind stone. And when Thor attacked him he just let him embed his axe in his chest instead of making the axe disappear, or the distance to him too far for Thor\u2019s momentum to carry him. He had infinite power over mind and he never just made his enemies agree with him.<br /> <br /> See what I mean that they seem inconsistent? Like, I can\u2019t be too hard on the writers, infinite power over anything is very difficult to work with. But that makes the whole premise of the Infinity War kind of doomed to these issues of \u201chow does Thanos ever fail if he can control reality? How does he ever get to control reality if the good guys control time?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> That becomes the issue with any &quot;fuck you, I win&quot; power set. When you have absolute power, your only real shortcoming is your own imagination. Two people wielding the Infinity Gauntlet might achieve dramatically different effects, depending on their personality and objective.<br /> <br /> <br /> As I think I mentioned previously, the reason why Thanos loses in the comics is because he subconsciously doesn't believe himself to be worthy enough, which has the effect of weakening his hold on the gems and allowing the heroes to steal his gauntlet.<br /> <br /> <br /> Another explanation is that the One Above All is allegedly the reason why nobody can ever keep their hands on the damn things for very long. The One Above All is not just some omnipotent being, he's a personification of the Marvel Writers, meaning he's the most powerful entity in the entire franchise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T07:41:13-07:00","id":1215488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1215294-avengers-infinity-war-spoiler-talk?p=1215486#post1215486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, no, I buy the whole \u201ckill half of everyone to stop overpopulation\u201d thing when he had to do it by invading planets with his armies. That makes sense as being the most effective method to a warped mind. The problem is that once he has the infinity gauntlet and all six stones, he could just as easily snap his fingers and halve everyone\u2019s resource consumption rate, double the resources in the universe, double the size of every planet, whatever he wants. To someone who can literally do anything they want, killing half the universe only really makes sense if his goal is to kill half the universe. Which it was in the comics. They changed his motive without changing his methods, and in so doing made his methods no longer make sense.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, that is indeed nonsensical... to clear minds like us who can still think rationally.<br /> <br /> I see MCU Thanos as essentially a one-man cult. (Well, the Black Order too, but they're more loyal to Thanos than to his ideas) And I've read and heard about too many cults to trust that the human mind is infallible, nor that it can fix itself so easily out of indoctrination just by being given a chance of introspection. (Well okay Thanos isn't human, and he's supposed to be much smarter than homo sapiens, but still.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T07:59:30-07:00","id":1215493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1215294-avengers-infinity-war-spoiler-talk?p=1215483#post1215483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, you can say he\u2019s just evil and really <b>wanted to kill half the universe</b></div> </div> </div> </div>That's literally the EXACT line Banner states in the movie. Literally, that. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T08:00:57-07:00","id":1215495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> 