rrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Willow is referring to when Thanos was using blasts of energy from the power stone in the fight on Titan.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Ah. Versus Tony. Got it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T08:32:30-07:00","id":1215505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1215294-avengers-infinity-war-spoiler-talk?p=1215488#post1215488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, that is indeed nonsensical... to clear minds like us who can still think rationally.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, so the answer to \u201cmovie Thanos seems like an idiot who doesn\u2019t know how to use his powers\u201d is, \u201che is.\u201d<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1215294-avengers-infinity-war-spoiler-talk?p=1215493#post1215493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's literally the EXACT line Banner states in the movie. Literally, that. </div> </div> </div> </div>Right, because he does want to kill half the universe. But it\u2019s framed as a means to an end, and it\u2019s a stupid means to the stated end of saving the universe from overpopulation. They want to frame Thanos as an \u201cends justify the means\u201d villain, but that doesn\u2019t work because he has better means to achieve the same ends. Thanos just doesn\u2019t work as the well-intentioned extremist the movie tries to sell him as. Either he\u2019s \u201cjust an idiot,\u201d which doesn\u2019t make him a very compelling villain, or he\u2019s just bloodthirsty and the overpopulation thing is an excuse, which doesn\u2019t come across as presented.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T08:42:01-07:00","id":1215509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1215294-avengers-infinity-war-spoiler-talk?p=1215505#post1215505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right, so the answer to \u201cmovie Thanos seems like an idiot who doesn\u2019t know how to use his powers\u201d is, \u201che is.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>I see you're optimistic about the infallible rationality of the mind. And is not afraid to label anyone who does not act according to standards of conventional rationality as having deficient intelligence, regardless of circumstances such as path dependence and self-rationalization, or perhaps is not afraid to define such mental biases as signs of less-than average intelligence.<br /> <br /> That's a ground I'd tread very carefully or not at all.<br /> <br /> <br /> ... Or maybe I'm a bit <i>too </i>familiar with cults and indoctrination and how the human mind does not work rationally, after having seen all the fundamentalist Christians, swindling shamans, fraudulent Taoists, and what can only be described as cults of personality in both ultra-conservative and radical progressive political parties. (And my recent efforts on 2E homebrew converions of the Secret Order of the Gate and the Cult of the Doomsday Clock does not help <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":".  last paragraph 05-05-2018, 11:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T08:53:19-07:00","id":1215512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1215294-avengers-infinity-war-spoiler-talk?p=1215509#post1215509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see you're optimistic about the infallible rationality of the mind. And is not afraid to label anyone who does not act according to standards of conventional rationality as having deficient intelligence, regardless of circumstances such as path dependence and self-rationalization, or perhaps is not afraid to define such mental biases as signs of less-than average intelligence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rather, I think \u201che didn\u2019t think of it\u201d is a narratively weak justification for a villain\u2019s actions, particularly when those actions have such dramatic consequences, and am not afraid to use hyperbole in my critique.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T09:05:45-07:00","id":1215518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1215294-avengers-infinity-war-spoiler-talk?p=1215512#post1215512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rather, I think \u201che didn\u2019t think of it\u201d is a narratively weak justification for a villain\u2019s actions, particularly when those actions have such dramatic consequences, and am not afraid to use hyperbole in my critique.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I see the part where you (and ArcaneArts) equated irrationality with idiocy as something that can\u2019t be glossed over as \u201cjust\u201d a hyperbole. Not anymore than using the word \u201cinsane\u201d as a synonym for \u201cevil\u201d can. <br /> <br /> On narrative weakness, I agree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T09:06:02-07:00","id":1215519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1215294-avengers-infinity-war-spoiler-talk?p=1215512#post1215512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rather, I think \u201che didn\u2019t think of it\u201d is a narratively weak justification for a villain\u2019s actions, particularly when those actions have such dramatic consequences, and am not afraid to use hyperbole in my critique.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Unfortunately, &quot;he didn't think of it&quot; is literally the only justification you can give in this situation. He had access to infinite power and control over nearly all aspects of the universe. If he failed to achieve his intended objective, the only possible explanation is that he didn't wield it to its full potential.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T09:09:52-07:00","id":1215523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1215294-avengers-infinity-war-spoiler-talk?p=1215519#post1215519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unfortunately, &amp;quot;he didn't think of it&amp;quot; is literally the only justification you can give in this situation. He had access to infinite power and control over nearly all aspects of the universe. If he failed to achieve his intended objective, the only possible explanation is that he didn't wield it to its full potential.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why I think changing his motive from \u201ckill half the universe for its own sake\u201d to \u201ckill half the universe to save the other half\u201d was a narratively poor choice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1215294-avengers-infinity-war-spoiler-talk?p=1215518#post1215518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I see the part where you (and ArcaneArts) equated irrationality with idiocy as something that can\u2019t be glossed over as \u201cjust\u201d a hyperbole. Not anymore than using the word \u201cinsane\u201d as a synonym for \u201cevil\u201d can. <br /> <br /> On narrative weakness, I agree.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough, I\u2019ll try to express myself better in this regard in the future.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T09:38:59-07:00","id":1215531,"title":"","content":"On a completely different note, I absolutely love that the new spidey suit has the Waldoes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T10:32:53-07:00","id":1215545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1215294-avengers-infinity-war-spoiler-talk?p=1215531#post1215531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a completely different note, I absolutely love that the new spidey suit has the Waldoes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I literally squealed in my seat when the waldoes came out the first time!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T11:28:26-07:00","id":1215560,"title":"","content":"It's not exactly related to the discussion, but I appreciated that Strange went from newbie wizard with a keen intellect and an Infinity Stone to Sorcerer Supreme without us having to wait another solo movie for that to happen.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T13:11:19-07:00","id":1215583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1215294-avengers-infinity-war-spoiler-talk?p=1215479#post1215479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> People in real life did more nonsensical things for less noble motives. I see no reason for Thanos to meet higher standards than what we give to fanatics all across the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I wanted realism, I would not be watching Avengers: Infinity War. I want narrative satisfaction, not excuses.<br /> <br /> Verisimilitude is not Realism, and Reality does not excuse a failure of Verisimilitude.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T14:55:28-07:00","id":1215600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1215294-avengers-infinity-war-spoiler-talk?p=1215583#post1215583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I wanted realism, I would not be watching Avengers: Infinity War. I want narrative satisfaction, not excuses.<br /> <br /> Verisimilitude is not Realism, and Reality does not excuse a failure of Verisimilitude.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hence my agreeing on narrative weakness and Thanos deserving a better fleshing out. <br /> <br /> And a continued disagreement with a casual dismissal of irrationality as idiocy. Not being satisfied does not give you a right to do that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T15:52:13-07:00","id":1215615,"title":"","content":"On the subject of why Strange couldn't use the Time Stone as Thanos did, I imagine it has to do with each stone being further empowered by the others. I mean, Thanos couldn't use the Reality Stone to change reality to one that only had half the people in it, or the Power Stone to just destroy half of the universe's population, and so on. He needed <b>all </b>the stones do murder half the universe.<br /> <br /> So, it appears to me that, for all that each Stone has supposed &quot;absolute&quot; power over their purview, they clearly have limitations.<br /> <br /> It is also possible that the Stones have unlimited potential in their area of effect, but the user's skill, willpower, or other capacities determine how much they can push out of them, and Thanos simply had more of whatever it is than Strange.<br /> <br /> Now, Thanos gauntlet was supposed to be able to channel the power of all the Gems, but it was pretty banged up after that half-of-everyone-is-gone finger snap. He might not have as much ability to tap into the Stones' power in the sequel, which may turn out as a reason why he doesn't easily turns the Avengers into fine powder when they confront him again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T15:58:03-07:00","id":1215616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1215294-avengers-infinity-war-spoiler-talk?p=1215615#post1215615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the subject of why Strange couldn't use the Time Stone as Thanos did, I imagine it has to do with each stone being further empowered by the others. I mean, Thanos couldn't use the Reality Stone to change reality to one that only had half the people in it, or the Power Stone to just destroy half of the universe's population, and so on. He needed <b>all </b>the stones do murder half the universe.<br /> <br /> So, it appears to me that, for all that each Stone has supposed &quot;absolute&quot; power over their purview, they clearly have limitations.<br /> <br /> It is also possible that the Stones have unlimited potential in their area of effect, but the user's skill, willpower, or other capacities determine how much they can push out of them, and Thanos simply had more of whatever it is than Strange.<br /> <br /> Now, Thanos gauntlet was supposed to be able to channel the power of all the Gems, but it was pretty banged up after that half-of-everyone-is-gone finger snap. He might not have as much ability to tap into the Stones' power in the sequel, which may turn out as a reason why he doesn't easily turns the Avengers into fine powder when they confront him again.</div> </div> </div> </div>That I would definitely buy, though I do wish it had been better established. Maybe in the next one.<br /> <br /> Also, in case I\u2019m coming off as overly critical, I did enjoy the movie quite a bit overall in spite of critiques related to the inherent problems with trying to write around objects of unlimited power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T16:33:11-07:00","id":1215622,"title":"","content":"I like Comics Thanos, he's one of my favorites. Movie Thanos is different and, while I prefer the comic version, I did like him too. Besides, Ultron is another of those I love, perhaps even more than Thanos (though Doom gets the top spot), so I've survived worse translations. I do agree that his motivation in the comics flows with less issues, but I think there's enough in-universe explanations behind how Movie Thanos acted the way he did<br /> <br /> To offer some speculation, based on me trying to get into Thanos' head:<br /> <br /> Thanos, in his twisted perspective, has no intention to provide infinite resources because that would require the one with all the Infinity Stones to stay around and shower people with food, materials and fuel, to keep things in check and become the benevolent god of a thankful universe. He does not want that: Movie Thanos wants to solve the Big Problem that torments him, willing to sacrifice everything in order to do that, be sure that the universe gains room to breath for a bunch of eras and retire, not giving a single fuck about being a space overlord, the hero of our dimension or anything like that. He wants to do that, retire and rest. Even die in due time. That's why he says he hoped Gamora would sit on his throne one day. Movie Thanos' is a different kind of egomaniac from Comic Thanos, in the sense he still believes that what he wants takes precedence over anything else, but in his mind the reasons to do so are less focused on him and more on a terrible greater good.<br /> <br /> We can speculate that those half-planet murders he did were his way to reach the goal before he learned about the Infinity Stones, or maybe something he kept doing because planets where dying out there and he had to step in and solve the issue, Stones or not. The armies, the tortures, the wars and all that stuff were means to an end.<br /> <br /> Now, he does this by killing, destroying, breaking minds and committing genocides on a cosmic scale, so I think we can all agree that's he's not a good guy, but I don't think he considers himself one either. Movie Thanos probably thinks of himself of the one who's strong enough both to recognize there's a fundamental flaw in the universe and to take on the weight of the feats and hard moral choices that are required to solve it.<br /> <br /> But I do believe his characterization implies that an &quot;unnatural&quot; solution such as becoming a neverending wellspring of resources would look to him as a naive way to solve things that might lead to disasters , conflicts and that would fall apart without someone taking care of everything all the time with the Infinity Stones. And Movie Thanos is <i>tired</i><br /> <br /> Having said that, I'm not gonna deny there's some narrative weakness in place and the MCU Mad Titan has irrationally tunnel-visioned himself into becoming the most dreaded being of the universe. That's why I said I hope we'll learn more about him in the next movie (in the other thread), because he's a cool antagonist that deserves better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 05-05-2018, 07:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T17:22:59-07:00","id":1215629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1215294-avengers-infinity-war-spoiler-talk?p=1215622#post1215622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like Comics Thanos, he's one of my favorites. Movie Thanos is different and, while I prefer the comic version, I did like him too. Besides, Ultron is another of those I love, perhaps even more than Thanos (though Doom gets the top spot), so I've survived worse translations. I do agree that his motivation in the comics flows with less issues, but I think there's enough in-universe explanations behind how Movie Thanos acted the way he did<br /> <br /> To offer some speculation, based on me trying to get into Thanos' head:<br /> <br /> Thanos, in his twisted perspective, has no intention to provide infinite resources because that would require the one with all the Infinity Stones to stay around and shower people with food, materials and fuel, to keep things in check and become the benevolent god of a thankful universe. He does not want that: Movie Thanos wants to solve the Big Problem that torments him, willing to sacrifice everything in order to do that, be sure that the universe gains room to breath for a bunch of eras and retire, not giving a single fuck about being a space overlord, the hero of our dimension or anything like that. He wants to do that, retire and rest. Even die in due time. That's why he says he hoped Gamora would sit on his throne one day. Movie Thanos' is a different kind of egomaniac from Comic Thanos, in the sense he still believes that what he wants takes precedence over anything else, but in his mind the reasons to do so are less focused on him and more on a terrible greater good.<br /> <br /> We can speculate that those half-planet murders he did were his way to reach the goal before he learned about the Infinity Stones, or maybe something he kept doing because planets where dying out there and he had to step in and solve the issue, Stones or not. The armies, the tortures, the wars and all that stuff were means to an end.<br /> <br /> Now, he does this by killing, destroying, breaking minds and committing genocides on a cosmic scale, so I think we can all agree that's he's not a good guy, but I don't think he considers himself one either. Movie Thanos probably thinks of himself of the one who's strong enough both to recognize there's a fundamental flaw in the universe and to take on the weight of the feats and hard moral choices that are required to solve it.<br /> <br /> But I do believe his characterization implies that an &quot;unnatural&quot; solution such as becoming a neverending wellspring of resources would look to him as a naive way to solve things that might lead to disasters , conflicts and that would fall apart without someone taking care of everything all the time with the Infinity Stones. And Movie Thanos is <i>tired</i><br /> <br /> Having said that, I'm not gonna deny there's some narrative weakness in place and the MCU Mad Titan has irrationally tunnel-visioned himself into becoming the most dreaded being of the universe. That's why I said I hope we'll learn more about him in the next movie (in the other thread), because he's a cool antagonist that deserves better.</div> </div> </div> </div>My problem with this take is that by any logic that would allow Thanos to rest after killing half of the people, he would also be able to rest after doubling the universe\u2019s resources once. Both have the same net result. Both are poor, temporary solutions to a highly localized problem being applied on a universal scale once. If he realizes that using the infinity stones to distribute resources where necessary would mean needing to perpetually act as a benevolent god, I find it hard to believe he wouldn\u2019t also realize that using them to cull the population where necessary would mean needing to perpetually act as a destroyer god.<br /> <br /> \u201cThe ends justify the means\u201d just cannot work as a motivation for a villain with unlimited means. If he has unlimited means, he can achieve his ends by means that require no justification. He just can. If he chooses to use unconscionable means <i>anyway</i> then his stated ends must not be his true ends. He must either be deceptive, if his stated ends are a smokescreen for his true ends, or delusional, if he actually believes his stated ends are his true ends. And this film has not sold me either explanation. I reserve the possibility that part 2 will redeem the character for me, but to do so, they would need to reveal that Thanos just straight-up wanted to kill half the people in the universe for its own sake, and that the overpopulation justification was a lie. It can be a lie he believed himself, but it must have been a lie for the character to make sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 05-05-2018, 08:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T19:21:45-07:00","id":1215652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1215294-avengers-infinity-war-spoiler-talk?p=1215629#post1215629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My problem with this take is that by any logic that would allow Thanos to rest after killing half of the people, he would also be able to rest after doubling the universe\u2019s resources once. Both have the <b>same net result</b>. Both are poor, temporary solutions to a highly localized problem being applied on a universal scale once. If he <b>realizes </b>that using the infinity stones to distribute resources where necessary would mean needing to perpetually act as a benevolent god, I find it hard to believe he wouldn\u2019t also realize that using them to cull the population where necessary would mean needing to perpetually act as a destroyer god.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, because you can't be a convincing villain without being <i>the</i> Rational Actor.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u201cThe ends justify the means\u201d just cannot work as a motivation for a villain with unlimited means. If he has unlimited means, he can achieve his ends by means that require no justification. He just can. If he chooses to use unconscionable means <i>anyway</i> then his stated ends must not be his true ends. He must either be deceptive, if his stated ends are a smokescreen for his true ends, or delusional, if he actually believes his stated ends are his true ends. And this film has not sold me either explanation. I reserve the possibility that part 2 will redeem the character for me, but to do so, they would need to reveal that Thanos just straight-up wanted to kill half the people in the universe for its own sake, and that the overpopulation justification was a lie. It can be a lie he believed himself, but it must have been a lie for the character to make sense. </div> </div> </div>By this point, I'm not sure what you want. Actually, I have a guess that all you want is the Comic Thanos to be on screen, without any compromise or reimagining whatsoever, but all your previous posts minus this thread tell me that you of all people can't be <i>that </i>shallow in motive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T20:23:44-07:00","id":1215666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1215294-avengers-infinity-war-spoiler-talk?p=1215652#post1215652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, because you can't be a convincing villain without being <i>the</i> Rational Actor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering one of my proposed fixes for the character is \u201che\u2019s delusional\u201d, I\u2019d think it would be clear that rational action is not an important factor for me. Like I said, I\u2019m fine if he <i>thinks</i> his goal is to save the universe. I just can\u2019t swallow that that\u2019s <i>actually</i> his goal, because if it was, he could have done so without killing half the people in it, and it\u2019s not like it takes a particularly rational or creative mind to realize that infinite power can save the universe in more ways than just killing half the people in it. Again, I buy that he\u2019s deluded enough to believe that killing half of a population could permanently save it from overpopulation. I just don\u2019t buy that he wouldn\u2019t realize the Infinity Gauntlet could be used to save the universe in a way that doesn\u2019t make him public enemy number 1 to all of the people he saves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1215294-avengers-infinity-war-spoiler-talk?p=1215652#post1215652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By this point, I'm not sure what you want. Actually, I have a guess that all you want is the Comic Thanos to be on screen, without any compromise or reimagining whatsoever,</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019ve never read the comics and have no horse in that race.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1215294-avengers-infinity-war-spoiler-talk?p=1215652#post1215652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but all your previous posts minus this thread tell me that you of all people can't be <i>that </i>shallow in motive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you, I think?<br /> <br /> What I want is a villain that the story paints as competent, and the story of this movie did not do that for Thanos. He wants to save the universe. He has unlimited power. And the best way he can think of to save the universe is to destroy half of it. That\u2019s not the behavior of a competent villain. That\u2019s the behavior of a miserably incompetent anti-hero. Unless saving the universe isn\u2019t really what he wants, or his power isn\u2019t really unlimited, but the movie didn\u2019t present it that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T20:49:28-07:00","id":1215670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1215294-avengers-infinity-war-spoiler-talk?p=1215666#post1215666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering one of my proposed fixes for the character is \u201che\u2019s delusional\u201d, I\u2019d think it would be clear that rational action is not an important factor for me. Like I said, I\u2019m fine if he <i>thinks</i> his goal is to save the universe. I just can\u2019t swallow that that\u2019s <i>actually</i> his goal, because if it was, he could have done so without killing half the people in it, and it\u2019s not like it takes a particularly rational or creative mind to realize that infinite power can save the universe in more ways than just killing half the people in it. Again, I buy that he\u2019s deluded enough to believe that killing half of a population could permanently save it from overpopulation. I just don\u2019t buy that he wouldn\u2019t realize the Infinity Gauntlet could be used to save the universe in a way that doesn\u2019t make him public enemy number 1 to all of the people he saves.<br /> <br /> <br /> I\u2019ve never read the comics and have no horse in that race.<br /> <br /> <br /> Thank you, I think?<br /> <br /> What I want is a villain that the story paints as competent, and the story of this movie did not do that for Thanos. He wants to save the universe. He has unlimited power. And the best way he can think of to save the universe is to destroy half of it. That\u2019s not the behavior of a competent villain. That\u2019s the behavior of a miserably incompetent anti-hero. Unless saving the universe isn\u2019t really what he wants, or his power isn\u2019t really unlimited, but the movie didn\u2019t present it that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Glad to hear. So I think we do agree on Thanos having deluded himself. And not on its implications. Eh, this veers into real-life philosophical conundrums, me thinks. Can\u2019t really resolve that. <br /> <br /> <br /> So, to continue with the movie - does anybody have an idea just what exactly is the Reality Stone\u2019s purview and potentials? I keep hearing something about Wyld Shaping when I peek at the Exalted forums - is it something similar, only applicable to the \u2018real\u2019 world?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T14:05:58-07:00","id":1215892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1215294-avengers-infinity-war-spoiler-talk?p=1215615#post1215615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the subject of why Strange couldn't use the Time Stone as Thanos did, I imagine it has to do with each stone being further empowered by the others. I mean, Thanos couldn't use the Reality Stone to change reality to one that only had half the people in it, or the Power Stone to just destroy half of the universe's population, and so on. He needed <b>all </b>the stones do murder half the universe.<br /> <br /> So, it appears to me that, for all that each Stone has supposed &quot;absolute&quot; power over their purview, they clearly have limitations.<br /> <br /> It is also possible that the Stones have unlimited potential in their area of effect, but the user's skill, willpower, or other capacities determine how much they can push out of them, and Thanos simply had more of whatever it is than Strange.<br /> <br /> Now, Thanos gauntlet was supposed to be able to channel the power of all the Gems, but it was pretty banged up after that half-of-everyone-is-gone finger snap. He might not have as much ability to tap into the Stones' power in the sequel, which may turn out as a reason why he doesn't easily turns the Avengers into fine powder when they confront him again.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> If Thanos wanted to empower the other gems, he only needed the Power Stone to do it, since one of its abilities in the comics is amplifying the infinite power of the other gems. Yeah, not sure how the hell you can amplify infinity, just roll with it.<br /> <br /> The reason why Strange couldn't do the same thing as Thanos is probably due to one of two factors.<br /> <br /> <b>Either A)</b> he didn't think of it - which seems incredibly unlikely given how he faced off against Dormomu<br /> <br /> <b>Or B)</b> - He wasn't strong enough to do so. - We've seen that it takes a very powerful being to even so much as touch the stones without being destroyed in the process. A Titan such as Thanos might just be more resilient than a human wizard like Strange","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T12:48:08-07:00","id":1216267,"title":"","content":"So I finally saw Infinity War an-<br /> <br /> *looks over whole thread*<br /> <br /> ...WOW you guys have been really going at it! Dayum. Imma need a moment to catch up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T22:00:00-07:00","id":1216899,"title":"","content":"I did my damnedest to avoid spoiling the ending for myself, prior to the movie. I avoided speculation threads, I avoided <i>this</i> thread.<br /> <br /> And then I walked by an <i>Infinity War</i> merch display, right before I was going to go see the movie. What do I see?<br /> <br /> The Infinity Gauntlet, with all six gems set into it.<br /> <br /> God<i>damn</i>it, Marvel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T22:13:21-07:00","id":1216901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1215294-avengers-infinity-war-spoiler-talk?p=1216899#post1216899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did my damnedest to avoid spoiling the ending for myself, prior to the movie. I avoided speculation threads, I avoided <i>this</i> thread.<br /> <br /> And then I walked by an <i>Infinity War</i> merch display, right before I was going to go see the movie. What do I see?<br /> <br /> The Infinity Gauntlet, with all six gems set into it.<br /> <br /> God<i>damn</i>it, Marvel.</div> </div> </div> </div>TO be fair, how were they going to merchandise it? Buy half now, buy half later?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T23:10:35-07:00","id":1216908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1215294-avengers-infinity-war-spoiler-talk?p=1216901#post1216901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">TO be fair, how were they going to merchandise it? Buy half now, buy half later?</div> </div> </div> </div>They already do that, like, all the time, so <i>yes.</i><br /> <br /> Alternatively, maybe change the packaging, so we don't see how many stones are fitted into it, at a glance, from ten feet away?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 05-09-2018, 02:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T23:27:17-07:00","id":1216911,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I\u2019m with Arc, even if Thanos <i>didnt</i> get all six in this movie, who\u2019s going to buy an Infinity Gauntlet toy with some of the stones missing?<br /> <br /> Also, that would kind of be even more of a spoiler. Imagine if Thanos had only gotten Power, Mind, Reality, and Space in this movie, and the display had the gauntlet with the Time and Soul stone missing. Then you\u2019d have known which ones Thanos got in this movie and which ones he was still missing by the end of it.<br /> <br /> I guess it could have been cool to sell a gauntlet with sockets the stones can snap into and the stones each separately.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 05-09-2018, 02:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T00:02:01-07:00","id":1216916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1215294-avengers-infinity-war-spoiler-talk?p=1216911#post1216911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess it could have been cool to sell a gauntlet with sockets the stones can snap into and the stones each separately.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what Lego did. One movie-related set has the Gauntlet and one stone, the other sets out for the movie have different stones in addition to whatever else.<br /> <br /> I don't think it's that big a spoiler, since merchandise doesn't always accurately represent what happens in the movie, and the gauntlet has already appeared in, I think, 2 movies, not to mention a comic storyline that has been selling decades for years and is so popular they apparently based a movie off of it.<br /> <br /> But obviously it's a subjective thing, I imagine reading the thread would spoil a lot more than seeing images of an artifact from the movie (I figured that part was obvious, it's the wiping out half the universe thing including some popular heroes that seems to be the big whammy of the movie).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-09-2018, 03:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T03:03:32-07:00","id":1216939,"title":"","content":"I also wanna say I agree with Willow from earlier - using a magic lamp to wish for a pinball machine is a pretty reasonable wish if what you want is a pinball machine\u2026 but if your stated goal for the wish was to bring about world peace, the number of <i>better</i> wishes you could have made may well be incalculable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 05-09-2018, 08:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T10:10:41-07:00","id":1217038,"title":"","content":"Personally, considering that the films change the basis for wielding the Infinity Stones from &quot;I just have them, and now I'm omnipotent&quot; to needing the Gauntlet as a piece of ancient Dwarf technology as an intermediary mechanism to the point that he literally needs to clench his fist to activate the powers, to the point that being physically restrained from doing so can inhibit him, as well as the depiction of how snapping his fingers causes the Gauntlet (and some of the arm wearing it) to become a charred mess, I'm inclined to read the visual language of the film as telling me that using the Stones in concert for the comparatively simple task of &quot;kill half the intelligent life in the universe&quot; was straining the Gauntlet to the limit, and that trying anything more complicated on a universal scale would have just made it, the wearer, and the surrounding landscape blow up without effectively achieving the desired effect.<br /> <br /> Apologies for the run-on sentence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T10:55:44-07:00","id":1217048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1215294-avengers-infinity-war-spoiler-talk?p=1217038#post1217038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, considering that the films change the basis for wielding the Infinity Stones from &quot;I just have them, and now I'm omnipotent&quot; to needing the Gauntlet as a piece of ancient Dwarf technology as an intermediary mechanism to the point that he literally needs to clench his fist to activate the powers, to the point that being physically restrained from doing so can inhibit him, as well as the depiction of how snapping his fingers causes the Gauntlet (and some of the arm wearing it) to become a charred mess, I'm inclined to read the visual language of the film as telling me that using the Stones in concert for the comparatively simple task of &quot;kill half the intelligent life in the universe&quot; was straining the Gauntlet to the limit, and that trying anything more complicated on a universal scale would have just made it, the wearer, and the surrounding landscape blow up without effectively achieving the desired effect.<br /> <br /> Apologies for the run-on sentence.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Except comic Thanos' goal is to kill all life in the universe in order to prove his love for Death. So really, blowing up the entire universe, including himself, would have been exactly the desired effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T11:09:34-07:00","id":1217054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1215294-avengers-infinity-war-spoiler-talk?p=1217048#post1217048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except comic Thanos' goal is to kill all life in the universe in order to prove his love for Death. So really, blowing up the entire universe, including himself, would have been exactly the desired effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>But that wasn\u2019t movie Thanos\u2019 goal, which is what we\u2019re discussing here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T11:47:28-07:00","id":1217068,"title":"","content":"Comic Infinity gems are pretty much limitless, too. If comic Thanos (or any wielder) wanted to make a world without cancer or whatever, they could do that. A bog-standard mortal with the Reality gem can change the universe so that certain characters (or all characters) never existed mere moments after holding onto it. So at least in the comics, there's little straining of the power as long as you're working within the confines of your universe.<br /> <br /> Based entirely on what I've heard, it sounds like the movie took some liberties to make a big show of things, as well as sort of abbreviating of the villain (cut the love of Death, make him omnicidal 'for good intentions' which fits the MCU). They're called stones in the movies, too, not gems as far as I can tell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":".  Inflammatory term 05-09-2018, 03:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T12:06:09-07:00","id":1217075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1215294-avengers-infinity-war-spoiler-talk?p=1217068#post1217068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Based entirely on what I've heard, it sounds like the movie took some liberties to make a big show of things, as well as sort of dumbing down of the villain (cut the love of Death, make him omnicidal 'for good intentions' which fits the MCU).</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI think these are the wrong terms to use; it adjusts the subjects to fit into the style and medium of the films. It's an adaptation, and that's no more taking liberties or dumbing down than is the fact that Tony Stark's origin story takes place in Afghanistan rather than Vietnam.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T12:21:14-07:00","id":1217079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1215294-avengers-infinity-war-spoiler-talk?p=1217075#post1217075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bI think these are the wrong terms to use; it adjusts the subjects to fit into the style and medium of the films. It's an adaptation, and that's no more taking liberties or dumbing down than is the fact that Tony Stark's origin story takes place in Afghanistan rather than Vietnam.</div> </div> </div> </div>Already fixed, it was poorly chosen, he's just had some pieces snipped off, like the Mandarin's ten science-magic rings or Ego not being a planet.<br /> <br /> I do think you have the wrong idea about it, though. This is not an attempt to tell a comic book story through movies. This is an attempt to make modern classics that will sustain Disney for the next several decades and give them household-name characters. These movies are so 10, 20 years down the line people talk about the Avengers the way they did/do Ghostbusters or Goonies or Star Wars. Any concerns about accurately portraying the print comics are going to be outweighed by the desire to tell a memorable story to a wider audience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-09-2018, 03:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T13:24:34-07:00","id":1217094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1215294-avengers-infinity-war-spoiler-talk?p=1217054#post1217054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But that wasn\u2019t movie Thanos\u2019 goal, which is what we\u2019re discussing here.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> True, and it definitely seems like his original comic book motivation would have been a hell of a lot better choice than what they went with.<br /> <br /> I mean, destroying half the universe's population won't stop them from running out of resources.<br /> <br /> It will just slow the rate at which they do so.<br /> <br /> Also, there's a little something called BREEDING, which means they'll eventually replenish their decimated numbers.<br /> <br /> Unless Thanos decides to purge half the universe every few millennia to keep the numbers down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T14:02:16-07:00","id":1217106,"title":"","content":"OK.... so the math of all this has bugged me a bit.<br /> <br /> People are saying that using the powers of the Gauntlet to create infinite resources (or something similar) is superior to culling life. But that just doesn't add up with the information we're provided.<br /> <br /> I'd also note that Thanos never says his intentions are just to wipe out sapient life forms. He always says life in general (which is actually far more a set back to repopulation).<br /> <br /> The important factors are (1) beings below Celestials - including Thanos - can't fully control the stones and their power has negative effects on those that try, and (2) unchecked population growth is exponential. If you use the Gauntlet to create vast resources for all of life, life will grow until it needs more resources. This is essential Thanos' whole problem with life in general. Life grows to the resources provided. In the comics continuity there's even a cancer-dimension where life was granted unlimited resources and the whole universe is just a giant mass of cancer like movie Ego took over but with Deadpool's body (in that story they actually defeat the cancer-dimension by tossing Thanos in it to kill it). If such a vast alteration is so draining, the Gauntlet users will not have to do it every few thousand years, they'd have to increase the universe's resources on an exponentially decreasing amount of time until eventually the Gauntlet will need a Celestial level entity to take this over (and they aren't prone to liking this kind of change unless it's their doing) because no lesser being could use it often enough to keep up with life growing and needing new resources.<br /> <br /> Culling is a drastically more effective solution (it's why we cull animals as a matter of conversation in real life).<br /> <br /> Cutting populations down to an &quot;ideal&quot; life is something that Thanos/Thanos' heirs (something he clearly recognizes he needs) can do once and awhile at a fairly regularly and stable interval. As well, life by it's nature adapts. If the universe gets purged every time there's too much life, life with shift to equalize close to that number. Space fairing societies will avoid colonization to avoid growing their numbers too high. etc.<br /> <br /> I'm not defending Thanos, and I appreciate the issues with the narrative provided, but the unlimited potential of the Gauntlet and stones doesn't mean it can be utilized perfectly. If the energy of utilizing the Gauntlet by a non-Celestial is limited (which it is as presented) trying to maintain an infinitely resource supplied universe can't handle it, eventually it's a worse result than leaving the resource levels as-is and culling.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T14:02:59-07:00","id":1217108,"title":"","content":"So hey, has this thread been <i>anything</i> but arguing over the viability of Thanos' motives and the depiction of the Infinity Gauntlet?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T14:41:38-07:00","id":1217128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1215294-avengers-infinity-war-spoiler-talk?p=1217106#post1217106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK.... so the math of all this has bugged me a bit.<br /> <br /> People are saying that using the powers of the Gauntlet to create infinite resources (or something similar) is superior to culling life. But that just doesn't add up with the information we're provided.<br /> <br /> I'd also note that Thanos never says his intentions are just to wipe out sapient life forms. He always says life in general (which is actually far more a set back to repopulation).<br /> <br /> The important factors are (1) beings below Celestials - including Thanos - can't fully control the stones and their power has negative effects on those that try, and (2) unchecked population growth is exponential. If you use the Gauntlet to create vast resources for all of life, life will grow until it needs more resources. This is essential Thanos' whole problem with life in general. Life grows to the resources provided. In the comics continuity there's even a cancer-dimension where life was granted unlimited resources and the whole universe is just a giant mass of cancer like movie Ego took over but with Deadpool's body (in that story they actually defeat the cancer-dimension by tossing Thanos in it to kill it). If such a vast alteration is so draining, the Gauntlet users will not have to do it every few thousand years, they'd have to increase the universe's resources on an exponentially decreasing amount of time until eventually the Gauntlet will need a Celestial level entity to take this over (and they aren't prone to liking this kind of change unless it's their doing) because no lesser being could use it often enough to keep up with life growing and needing new resources.<br /> <br /> Culling is a drastically more effective solution (it's why we cull animals as a matter of conversation in real life).<br /> <br /> Cutting populations down to an &quot;ideal&quot; life is something that Thanos/Thanos' heirs (something he clearly recognizes he needs) can do once and awhile at a fairly regularly and stable interval. As well, life by it's nature adapts. If the universe gets purged every time there's too much life, life with shift to equalize close to that number. Space fairing societies will avoid colonization to avoid growing their numbers too high. etc.<br /> <br /> I'm not defending Thanos, and I appreciate the issues with the narrative provided, but the unlimited potential of the Gauntlet and stones doesn't mean it can be utilized perfectly. If the energy of utilizing the Gauntlet by a non-Celestial is limited (which it is as presented) trying to maintain an infinitely resource supplied universe can't handle it, eventually it's a worse result than leaving the resource levels as-is and culling.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> All of which, the stones would be perfectly capable of achieving. They aren't called the <i>&quot;infinity stones / gems&quot;</i> because they thought it would sound cool. Their power is supposed to be <b>literally infinite</b> within the confines of their universe and the purviews they govern. Once you obtained the Reality Stone, you could rewrite the universe into anything you wanted and just straight up decide <i>&quot;The universe has enough resources for everybody. Period, end of discussion!&quot; </i>and if you weren't strong, or smart enough to handle that kind of alteration, the Power and Mind stones have you covered on that.<br /> <br /> <br /> Heck, you could even use the Time stone to replenish all the resources that have been used up, just like Strange used it to replenish an apple he had consumed.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T14:45:10-07:00","id":1217129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1215294-avengers-infinity-war-spoiler-talk?p=1217108#post1217108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So hey, has this thread been <i>anything</i> but arguing over the viability of Thanos' motives and the depiction of the Infinity Gauntlet?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really but everyone seems to like the movie otherwise, it just seems to be a sticking point for some.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T16:01:46-07:00","id":1217171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1215294-avengers-infinity-war-spoiler-talk?p=1217108#post1217108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So hey, has this thread been <i>anything</i> but arguing over the viability of Thanos' motives and the depiction of the Infinity Gauntlet?</div> </div> </div> </div>Once I see it this weekend, I can comment. Jeff Thew of Mother's Basement says it's pretty brilliant story-craft, so I still have hopes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T16:19:55-07:00","id":1217178,"title":"","content":"Ok...imma go things one at a time.<br /> <br /> So the other thing people have been arguing about is:<br /> <br /> <i><b>&quot;Why didn't Doctor Strange stop Peter from ruining everything?&quot;</b></i><br /> <br /> Well...for me, this gets into subjective territory but the way how I see it:<br /> <br /> I think Doctor Strange was lying when he said he saw 1 possibility out of 14 million timelines to beat Thanos. I think what he actually saw was 0.<br /> <br /> My evidence being:<ul><li>Strange hesitating when he gets asked how many timelines did he see where they won.</li> <li>Him going back on his earlier statement of &quot;choosing to protect the Gem over saving any of [their] lives&quot; by choosing to bargain for Iron Man's life for the Gem.</li> <li>And his statement to Iron Man on &quot;This was the only way!&quot;</li> </ul><br /> That he knew from the start that there was no way they could keep the Time Gem away from Thanos. And that Peter losing his head at the wrong moment was just one of many. And probably among those timelines was him trying to stop Peter, and it failing.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Why couldn't he just sit Peter out of the whole operation?&quot; </i><br /> <br /> Then there would be one less body in the plan, and capturing Thanos at all would have been much more difficult. And the rest of team would have questioned Strange on why he was sitting out Peter. Either he explains what happens...and they waste time and Thanos beats them. Or he doesn't tell them, they get confused on why he left him out, they're not operating at 100%, and Thanos wins.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Why didn't he try to stop Peter in that very moment?&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Same as above: doesn't matter if he used the Time Gem right there and then (which in of itself would have exposed its location to Thanos) or if he sent his cape to stop Peter, to the rest of the team, they'll think Strange has lost it because he attacked one of their own. Either they'll stand their ground and look confused, or they'll stop what they're doing and try to restrain Strange from out of nowhere team-killing. That distracts them from Thanos, and Thanos wins.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;If he knew they couldn't win, why go with a plan at all?&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Because you know...what else was he going to say to the others? Would YOU tell them that they have 0 chance in winning, or would you try to keep hope alive by saying that there's at least *a* chance? I would.<br /> <br /> To bring this back to TRPGs...won't you think it's shitty/bullshit if you and your party comes up with a plan and your DM/GM/ST flat out tells you: &quot;Ok then...there's no point though, you guys are going to fail anyways, no matter what you do&quot;?<br /> <br /> ...so unless if people are saying that Strange should have meditated longer and investigated 15 or 16 million timelines instead of just the 14 million.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4418,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","user":"tasti man LH","date":". 05-09-2018, 07:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T16:49:37-07:00","id":1217188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1215294-avengers-infinity-war-spoiler-talk?p=1217128#post1217128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All of which, the stones would be perfectly capable of achieving.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which I addressed. The stones <b>could</b>, but the user isn't guaranteed to be able to. It is made repeatedly clear across the movies that how much of the infinite potential of the stones a single individual (at least below Celestial level) can tap into is a variable, and has negative consequences on the user if they push too hard.<br /> <br /> Thanos, as a flawed creature, can't harness the stones to create a perfect universe, so he creates a universe that is, from his perspective, better.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Once you obtained the Reality Stone, you could rewrite the universe into anything you wanted and just straight up decide <i>&quot;The universe has enough resources for everybody. Period, end of discussion!&quot; </i>and if you weren't strong, or smart enough to handle that kind of alteration, the Power and Mind stones have you covered on that. </div> </div> </div>The movie versions clearly don't follow the comics in this regard.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Heck, you could even use the Time stone to replenish all the resources that have been used up, just like Strange used it to replenish an apple he had consumed. </div> </div> </div>This doesn't negate the math issue. If the energy demands needed for a non-Celestial level entity to operate the stones grows beyond their ability to handle it, it malfunctions. Replenishing an apple is clearly well within Strange's abilities. Where's the sign that Strange could do that for every metabolic resource used in the entire universe, all the time?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T17:03:39-07:00","id":1217192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1215294-avengers-infinity-war-spoiler-talk?p=1217108#post1217108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So hey, has this thread been <i>anything</i> but arguing over the viability of Thanos' motives and the depiction of the Infinity Gauntlet?</div> </div> </div> </div>There have been a few random posts of things like \u201cso, Spider-Man has Waldoes now, that\u2019s cool.\u201d But generally, Thanos\u2019 motives have been one of very few contentious points, and therefore one of very few interesting discussion topics.<br /> <br /> You and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> raise some excellent points, which make me think the issue might be less with Thanos\u2019 motivation and more with the vaguely-defined capabilities of the Infinity Gauntlet and stones.<br /> <br /> Anyway, to maybe shift the topic a little but... Is anyone else worried that this storyline might harm the dramatic tension for the MCU overall? I mean, I wasn\u2019t emotionally impacted as hard as I might have been by half the cast getting killed because I know they\u2019ll all be back by the end of part two except maybe Vision and Gamora. I wouldn\u2019t want death to lose its impact in the broader MCU as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 05-09-2018, 08:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T17:10:54-07:00","id":1217195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1215294-avengers-infinity-war-spoiler-talk?p=1217178#post1217178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok...imma go things one at a time.<br /> <br /> So the other thing people have been arguing about is:<br /> <br /> <i><b>&amp;quot;Why didn't Doctor Strange stop Peter from ruining everything?&amp;quot;</b></i><br /> <br /> Well...for me, this gets into subjective territory but the way how I see it:<br /> <br /> I think Doctor Strange was lying when he said he saw 1 possibility out of 14 million timelines to beat Thanos. I think what he actually saw was 0.<br /> <br /> My evidence being:<ul><li>Strange hesitating when he gets asked how many timelines did he see where they won.</li> <li>Him going back on his earlier statement of &amp;quot;choosing to protect the Gem over saving any of [their] lives&amp;quot; by choosing to bargain for Iron Man's life for the Gem.</li> <li>And his statement to Iron Man on &amp;quot;This was the only way!&amp;quot;</li> </ul><br /> That he knew from the start that there was no way they could keep the Time Gem away from Thanos. And that Peter losing his head at the wrong moment was just one of many. And probably among those timelines was him trying to stop Peter, and it failing.<br /> <br /> <i>&amp;quot;Why couldn't he just sit Peter out of the whole operation?&amp;quot; </i><br /> <br /> Then there would be one less body in the plan, and capturing Thanos at all would have been much more difficult. And the rest of team would have questioned Strange on why he was sitting out Peter. Either he explains what happens...and they waste time and Thanos beats them. Or he doesn't tell them, they get confused on why he left him out, they're not operating at 100%, and Thanos wins.<br /> <br /> <i>&amp;quot;Why didn't he try to stop Peter in that very moment?&amp;quot;</i><br /> <br /> Same as above: doesn't matter if he used the Time Gem right there and then (which in of itself would have exposed its location to Thanos) or if he sent his cape to stop Peter, to the rest of the team, they'll think Strange has lost it because he attacked one of their own. Either they'll stand their ground and look confused, or they'll stop what they're doing and try to restrain Strange from out of nowhere team-killing. That distracts them from Thanos, and Thanos wins.<br /> <br /> <i>&amp;quot;If he knew they couldn't win, why go with a plan at all?&amp;quot;</i><br /> <br /> Because you know...what else was he going to say to the others? Would YOU tell them that they have 0 chance in winning, or would you try to keep hope alive by saying that there's at least *a* chance? I would.<br /> <br /> To bring this back to TRPGs...won't you think it's shitty/bullshit if you and your party comes up with a plan and your DM/GM/ST flat out tells you: &amp;quot;Ok then...there's no point though, you guys are going to fail anyways, no matter what you do&amp;quot;?<br /> <br /> ...so unless if people are saying that Strange should have meditated longer and investigated 15 or 16 million timelines instead of just the 14 million.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, none of this explains why, once they had Thanos restrained, Strange didn\u2019t use a portal to cut off his arm like they did to the one big guy earlier in the movie instead of trying to pull the glove off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T17:19:20-07:00","id":1217201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1215294-avengers-infinity-war-spoiler-talk?p=1217195#post1217195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Of course, none of this explains why, once they had Thanos restrained, Strange didn\u2019t use a portal to cut off his arm like they did to the one big guy earlier in the movie instead of trying to pull the glove off.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm left with the impression that Thanos is a lot more durable to be easily dis-armed.<br /> <br /> Considering that he took Thor's shiny new axe to the chest and wasn't insta-killed by it.<br /> <br /> ...or that when they attempt to pick up the Gauntlet, someone accidentally touches one of the Gems, gets incinerated by it, distracts everyone, Thanos gets the gauntlet back, and they're back to square one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T18:00:02-07:00","id":1217211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1215294-avengers-infinity-war-spoiler-talk?p=1217192#post1217192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanos\u2019 motives have been one of very few contentious points, and therefore one of very few interesting discussion topics.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI don't know; over on RPGnet, we have a side thread devoted entirely to pointing out little things that people enjoyed, that's about six times longer than this thread is. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (I am 100% aware that the RPGnet community, including in its Other Media forum, is far larger than this one)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> raise some excellent points, which make me think the issue might be less with Thanos\u2019 motivation and more with the vaguely-defined capabilities of the Infinity Gauntlet and stones.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI think that it's an opportunity cost thing; the film is already very long, and has to juggle a very large cast of characters (quite possibly the biggest of any blockbuster movie ever), as well as introducing some new ones and introducing a few additional concepts. As plot devices and as active components of the film, the Infinity Stones are certainly important, but there's just limited room to include much explanation for the exact parameters of their powers, and I can see them as taking the lowest priority in an already weighty film.<br /> <br /> \u200bI think the manner in which the film ultimately portrays them is a compromise, but a necessary and well-crafted one; if they can't be heavily explained, then just show them in use, sufficient to convey the basics to an audience that is presumably already drawn in for the ride, and enough to extrapolate for somebody that wants deeper analysis.<br /> <br /> \u200bSo I think that it's enough for the film to show the Infinity Stones in use and allow one to determine the limits of their uses (in concert with what we see of Thanos' personality and capabilities). I don't think that there's anything blatantly contradictory enough to invalidate the depiction. I do think it requires a bit of buy-in from the audience, but I don't think that's necessarily a bad thing, and when getting into subjects of extreme supernatural power, is kind of necessary.<br /> <br /> \u200bOverall, I found the portrayal of Thanos and the presentation of the Infinity Stones (especially in the use of powers to create a thrilling and inventive action sequence, one of the best that I've ever seen, and certainly one that best utilised the premise that people on both sides were basically wizards) sufficiently compelling and well made that I'm willing to extend the film the benefit of the doubt regarding any minor inconsistencies. Like, in the fight scene on Titan, if Thanos is ever not using a Stone to the same extent that he has another time, or that it would be theoretically capable of, I'm willing to frame that as limitations arising from Thanos still being mortal and being pressed to his limit by the relentless and varied attacks being levelled at him, such that he's being driven by combat intuition and improvisation rather than having full recourse to consider application of the power down to the finest detail*.<br /> <br /> \u200bI'm willing to give it that, because it's never not boring. The first thing he does in that battle is blow up a ship and then transfigure the debris into a flock of winged animals to attack Iron Man! That alone makes it instantly more interesting than anything that ever happened in a Harry Potter film.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is anyone else worried that this storyline might harm the dramatic tension for the MCU overall? I mean, I wasn\u2019t emotionally impacted as hard as I might have been by half the cast getting killed because I know they\u2019ll all be back by the end of part two except maybe Vision and Gamora. I wouldn\u2019t want death to lose its impact in the broader MCU as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's going to depend a bit on how the next Avengers film handles the challenge of it, but I would also find it highly credible for the trajectory of this narrative to go with characters resolving that the Infinity Stones represent too much power to ever allow anybody to have a chance at them again, which is placed as a higher priority than having access to a permanent reset button.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat they might have recourse to undo this one extreme, but that's all they ever get; the danger is too great to allow, and it's never a power that they'll have again.<br /> <br /> \u200bOr maybe the Living Tribunal will just turn up to take it away when they're done, I don't know. <br /> <br /> \u200b* If he'd had the Mind Stone, that might have been a basis for thinking that his own mental capabilities could have been enhanced to more effectively use other Stones. Mind being the last he gets probably owes a lot more to the dramatic significance of killing Vision for it, but it would be a happy coincidence in resolving such an issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T18:16:26-07:00","id":1217218,"title":"","content":"Not to mention it becomes a bit of a creative dead end whenever you have any storyline that involves granting someone unlimited power or time travel.<br /> <br /> Because &quot;Why didn't this character just use unlimited power to kill all of his enemies at once?&quot;...doesn't make for an interesting story.<br /> <br /> That the only real solution is &quot;don't have stories that involve people getting granted unlimited power or time travel&quot;...which in this case, it would come down to &quot;Then Marvel Studios shouldn't have had Thanos and the Infinity Gems be their big metaplot in the first place&quot;.<br /> <br /> Like, I consider Back to the Future to be the best time-travel story of all time...and people STILL find reasons to poke holes in it, to find any proof that &quot;their time travel rules don't make sense&quot; or &quot;why they didn't think of doing this if they have time travel?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4418,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","user":"tasti man LH","date":". 05-09-2018, 09:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T18:19:03-07:00","id":1217219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1215294-avengers-infinity-war-spoiler-talk?p=1217192#post1217192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, to maybe shift the topic a little but... Is anyone else worried that this storyline might harm the dramatic tension for the MCU overall? I mean, I wasn\u2019t emotionally impacted as hard as I might have been by half the cast getting killed because I know they\u2019ll all be back by the end of part two except maybe Vision and Gamora. I wouldn\u2019t want death to lose its impact in the broader MCU as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure it harms the tension for the MCU in general, because it's extremely unlikely for the Infinity Gauntlet to stay something accessible to the rest of the movies. I think it hurt this specific movie, because I don't know anyone that buys Marvel trying to claim that they're not going to in-universe retcon things (esp. with multiple characters that either were slating for more films or Marvel would be stupid to not make more films with). But the stones will be destroyed or locked away again, so death in general will remain a meaningful consequence in the overall franchise.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T18:36:04-07:00","id":1217223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1215294-avengers-infinity-war-spoiler-talk?p=1217192#post1217192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, to maybe shift the topic a little but... Is anyone else worried that this storyline might harm the dramatic tension for the MCU overall? I mean, I wasn\u2019t emotionally impacted as hard as I might have been by half the cast getting killed because I know they\u2019ll all be back by the end of part two except maybe Vision and Gamora. I wouldn\u2019t want death to lose its impact in the broader MCU as well.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1215294-avengers-infinity-war-spoiler-talk?p=1217219#post1217219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure it harms the tension for the MCU in general, because it's extremely unlikely for the Infinity Gauntlet to stay something accessible to the rest of the movies. I think it hurt this specific movie, because I don't know anyone that buys Marvel trying to claim that they're not going to in-universe retcon things (esp. with multiple characters that either were slating for more films or Marvel would be stupid to not make more films with). But the stones will be destroyed or locked away again, so death in general will remain a meaningful consequence in the overall franchise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Amusingly, <a href=\"https://www.polygon.com/2018/5/9/17326608/avengers-infinity-war-ending-deaths-viewed-for-kids\" target=\"_blank\">Polygon released an article related to the subject</a>...specifically on adult fan's perspective versus a child fan's. Which...sort of puts things into perspective about the other audience members.<br /> <br /> Now while I don't buy that all of these deaths are permanent, I at least appreciate the the in-movie impact and presentation of the ending not to be mad at it.<br /> <br /> ...also, James Gunn confirmed awhile ago that GotG vol 3 is going to center around Gamora. So unless if he was completely bullshiting everyone...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T19:05:19-07:00","id":1217233,"title":"","content":"Which is entirely possible. Gunn requested Yondu's actor show up in full makeup on the set of Ragnarok and had an Infinity War cap made for him just to throw fans off the scent of Vol. 2's ending. Marvel trolls their fans hard to keep them second guessing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T21:22:32-07:00","id":1217262,"title":"","content":"I do get the point about kids, but it's a PG-13 movie, and I'd imagine most 10-15 year olds that have watched enough of the previous movies to care about the characters that got killed are going to have more of the adult reaction; I would have back then since I'd already realized death was cheap in comics and franchise movies by that point. There's certainly part of the audience still in the group that's invested enough to care, and not desensitized to comic book narratives, that are going to have the &quot;kid&quot; reaction in the article. I'm just not convinced it's that generational.<br /> <br /> The impact of the deaths was really on the actors because they sold those deaths as real to their characters beyond what the sequel will do. I thought a lot of performances in the finale were fantastic at managing a perfect balance of horror and being numbed by the anticlimactic nature of everyone just dusting away instead of epic battle deaths. The sheer disbelief that it was really that easy for Thanos to kill them like that, or the resignation in those that had accepted it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T22:43:45-07:00","id":1217278,"title":"","content":"One thing that'll be interesting to see is if those deaths matter, not in the usual terms of raising stakes and changing tone, but as character shock moments. After all, some of these deaths follow after some incredibly potent tragedies, which compounds the shock of, you know, dying. So if the movie can convince that these deaths are gonna be a thing moving forward...well, that'll be cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T02:14:41-07:00","id":1217301,"title":"","content":"There's definitely deaths that seem easier to be story fodder even if undone. Spider-man for both Peter and Tony should be a big one, since it can be a reason to get Tony to unclench in his role as a mentor, and is a good catalyst for Peter maturing in a more nuanced way than repeating the &quot;with great power comes great responsibility&quot; lesson.<br /> <br /> Gamora is the only one of the Guardians that seems like her death is really going to have a strong impact, but she died differently than the rest. We've already had a &quot;Groot dies&quot; beat in GotG vol. 1, making it really hard to make him going land hard.<br /> <br /> Strange and T'Challa both died repeatedly in their stand alone movies (well, T'Challa did a spiritual journey to the ancestral plane twice, and was tossed of a cliff to show up alive later once compared to Strange actually dying but reversing it a lot), so it's really hard to give them much weight. Bucky dying and coming back was already a big emotional beat for Winter Soldier (and Fury to an extent), and takes some of the potential impact of Sam's death because it's just repeating Cap loosing another best friend/fellow soldier.<br /> <br /> Wanda's one of the only Avengers core group that seems to have a lot of potential because she both dies and loses Vision... her powerlessness could very easily justify her growing closer to her comic book powers as part of an emotional arc to avoid that happening again.<br /> <br /> The Thor/Asgard group has some potential, but we're probably not getting a fourth Thor to resolve it (but it could be cool if Thor becomes the Iron Man/Nick Fury to a wider array of cosmic MCU with Guardians, and using the destruction of Xandar to introduce the Nova Force and get Nova into things, plus Adam Warlock as teased in GotG vol 2, and all that). They really set up Thor for the cyclical Asgard in the comics... but it doesn't seem like we're going to see a pay off even if Loki and Heimdall (all both characters we already had 'thought they were dead' moments before) come back. Or that becomes part of Dr. Strange 2 or 3 after Thor runs around the galaxy a bit and decides to resurrect Asgard in a pocket dimension attached to Earth. Thor's story has a lot of potential with however he reconciles who he's supposed to be with what happened in Ragnarock and Infinity War.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T07:27:41-07:00","id":1217389,"title":"","content":"&quot;I wonder about the thing.&quot;<br /> \u200b&quot;Allow me to give you my opinion about the thing before you even see it, creating a bias.&quot;<br /> <br /> Silly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T14:21:34-07:00","id":1217495,"title":"","content":"Eh? It's a spoiler discussion, worrying about creating preconceptions seems silly.<br /> <br /> Also, a large part of my point is that we've already seen the thing from Marvel, which is what guides a lot of that bias. We've seen Bucky 'die' and come back. We've seen Loki and Heimdall get 'killed.' We've seen Groot's heroic sacrifice. We've seen Black Panther stabbed in the gut and tossed off a cliff. We've seen Fury get shot and pronounced dead only to come back later having faked it. We've seen Doctor Strange let himself get killed (repeatedly) to beat a being beyond human power.<br /> <br /> Discussing what potential there is in narratives from the deaths of characters in the plot of Infinity War even if all the deaths are undone in the end can't be had in a vacuum of the way the MCU has already handled characters dying and coming back from the audience/character perspective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T15:48:36-07:00","id":1217512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1215294-avengers-infinity-war-spoiler-talk?p=1217389#post1217389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;I wonder about the thing.&quot;<br /> \u200b&quot;Allow me to give you my opinion about the thing before you even see it, creating a bias.&quot;<br /> <br /> Silly.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is, in fact, what I was asking for.<br /> <br /> You know me well enough to know I already have biases, and that when I go looking for biases of others, I am so doing in order to combat those biases.<br /> <br /> It's either that or I go in determined to see things my way, which is <i>not a good thing for this movie</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T16:04:07-07:00","id":1217518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1215294-avengers-infinity-war-spoiler-talk?p=1217512#post1217512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">which is <i>not a good thing for this movie</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the movie will be just fine. No worries. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T17:34:49-07:00","id":1217539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1215294-avengers-infinity-war-spoiler-talk?p=1217512#post1217512\" rel=\"nofo